    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1232">

                <pb facs="1054" n="950" sameAs="frus:frus1913/pg950"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 412.00/28a.</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the
                            American Ambassador.</hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram—Paraphrase.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Department of State</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1913-08-25">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">August 25, 1913</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>What claims, if any, of foreign governments against Mexico have been paid, in
                    part or in full, since the beginning of Madero’s administration? What were the
                    amounts thereof? What was the amount of the Covadonga award? Has it been
                    paid?</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Bryan</hi>.</signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
